{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>For in his city of refuge he shall dwell until the death of the high priest.</b> Peshat: so that people will not murmur against the high priest when they see the murderer going outside his city of refuge, saying: See this one who killed a person, and there is no high priest taking vengeance against him — and upon him the matter falls, as it is written: ובאת אל הכהן אשר יהיה בימים ההם. But when the high priest dies there is no need to be concerned about the priest who comes after him, for what would they murmur against him, seeing that it did not happen in his days?"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:31.964545049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}